{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And he said.</b> Before beginning the blessing that opens with ״בַּרְזֶל וּנְחֹשֶׁת מִנְעָלֶיךָ״ (Deuteronomy 33:25), he said this introduction and prayed on behalf of the tribes, in order that his blessing might take effect. For indeed words of blessing in every case address the one being blessed, as it says: ״אָמוֹר לָהֶם״ (Numbers 6:23). And so all his words from ״בַּרְזֶל וּנְחֹשֶׁת״ (Deuteronomy 33:25) through ״עַל בָּמוֹתֵימוֹ תִדְרֹךְ״ (Deuteronomy 33:29) were directed to Israel, but his preceding words were directed to the El, to petition Him on behalf of His people." "<b>YHWH.</b> An expression of address." "<b>From Sinai He came and shone forth… a fiery law for them.</b> He recalled the merit of Israel so that his prayer on their behalf would be accepted and his blessing would take effect, and he said to the El, blessed be He: Behold, from Sinai He came and shone forth and appeared from various places to Israel with the holiness of a fiery law, which is the intellective portion that comes from myriads of holiness, from the right side of holiness — for indeed it was given through the illuminating speculum."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:23:31.486072220Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}